---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { FUNI_URL, GITHUB_MOD, ORG, PRODUCT } from '../consts';
---

<PageLayout
	title="About"
	description="About KSC Tower Network — multiplayer ATC for Kerbal Space Program from Funi Labs."
>
	<section class="page-hero">
		<div class="shell">
			<h1>About</h1>
			<p>
				{PRODUCT} turns KSP into a multi-machine air-traffic-control sandbox for community
				role-play and ops practice.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section" style="padding-top: 0;">
		<div class="shell prose">
			<h2>The idea</h2>
			<p>
				One person flies. Another works tower. They share a radio, a map, and a strip —
				not a physics server. That keeps KSP feel intact while unlocking real ATC
				coordination across machines.
			</p>

			<h2>Who builds it</h2>
			<p>
				{PRODUCT} is developed under <a href={FUNI_URL}>{ORG}</a>. The mod sources live on
				GitHub; this site is the public front door at ksctower.com.
			</p>

			<h2>Roadmap flavor</h2>
			<p>
				Beyond today’s voice, telemetry, ACARS, and hull-cam desk, the longer plan leans into
				deeper tower ops: per-frequency channels, ATIS loops, flight strips, handoff,
				ghost traffic, and multi-seat roles like ground and approach.
			</p>

			<h2>License &amp; game</h2>
			<p>
				The client is aimed at KSP 1.12.x and is documented for MIT-style distribution via
				CKAN when releases are published. Kerbal Space Program is a trademark of its
				respective owners — this project is an unofficial community mod and is not affiliated
				with or endorsed by Intercept Games / Take-Two.
			</p>

			<div class="cta-row" style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">
				<a class="btn btn-primary" href={GITHUB_MOD} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"
					>Mod repository</a
				>
				<a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/get-started">Get started</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</PageLayout>
